\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\b\fs32 VUE 3D Canvas - Windows Compilation & Build Guide\cf0\b0\fs22\par
\b Author / Creator:\b0  Victory Ukpong\par
\b Target Architecture:\b0  Rust (Core/Logic) + WASM-first + Native Windows Desktop (DirectX 11 / OpenGL 2.0 Fallback)\par
\b Core Constraints:\b0  Low memory footprint, max 3 undo states in .xblend, linked assets by default, no ray-tracing or D3D12 dependency.\par
\par
\hr\par
\cf1\b\fs26 1. System Requirements\cf0\b0\fs22\par
- OS: Windows 10 (64-bit) or Windows 11\par
- RAM: 4 GB minimum (optimized for low-end hardware)\par
- GPU: DirectX 11 or OpenGL 2.0 capable graphics card\par
- Build Prerequisites: Node.js (v18+ or v20+ LTS), Rust Toolchain (rustup-init.exe, MSVC x64), Visual Studio C++ Build Tools.\par
\par
\cf1\b\fs26 2. Option A: Web / WASM-First Build (Quickest Execution)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
1. Open PowerShell in project directory:\par
{\f1\cf3   cd C:\\path\\to\\vue-3d-canvas\par
  npm install\par
  npm run dev\par}\par
2. Open http://localhost:3000 in your web browser.\par
3. To generate production distribution bundle:\par
{\f1\cf3   npm run build\par}\par
\par
\cf1\b\fs26 3. Option B: Standalone Native Windows Application (.exe via Tauri)\cf0\b0\fs22\par
1. Install Tauri CLI:\par
{\f1\cf3   npm install --save-dev @tauri-apps/cli\par}\par
2. Build standalone executable:\par
{\f1\cf3   npm run build\par
  npx tauri build\par}\par
3. Output executable location:\par
{\f1\cf3   src-tauri\\target\\release\\VUE 3D Canvas.exe\par}\par
\par
\cf1\b\fs26 4. Digital Stylus Tablet & Wintab Driver Notes\cf0\b0\fs22\par
- Enable Windows Ink in your tablet driver settings (Wacom, Huion, XP-Pen).\par
- In VUE 3D Canvas, enable "Touch Nav". Single touch finger navigates (pans and zooms 3D and 2D UV view), while stylus pen draws directly with pressure and tilt.\par
\par
\cf1\b\fs26 5. 2D UV Texture Map & Overlay Features\cf0\b0\fs22\par
- Switch between 3D View, Split 3D+UV, and 2D UV Map using the top view mode switcher.\par
- In 2D UV view, toggle the "UV Overlay: ON/OFF" button to display the flattened 3D model wireframe mesh.\par
- Multi-touch pinch-to-zoom and two-finger pan are fully supported on touchscreens.\par
\par
